id: pm-gh1647
title: "GH-1647: acquireLock / acquireLockLease follow a symlinked locks directory and create the lock outside the tracker"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1647 (found by pm-rl's state-confinement guarantee, unbraind/pm-rl#107): when the tracker's locks directory (or a lock entry's parent) is a symlink, acquireLock and acquireLockLease follow it and create the lock outside the tracker, so two writers resolving the path differently share no exclusion point and an extension cannot close the check/use window with its own pathname check. The SDK must refuse a symlinked or swapped lock directory with a typed lock_path_unsafe error and never create a lock outside the tracker."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: bug,concurrency,"gh:1647",locks,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T13:54:38.490Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:25.492Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:25.492Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "acquireLock and acquireLockLease refuse with code lock_path_unsafe when the tracker's locks directory, or any component between the tracker root and the lock entry, is a symlink or not a directory, and no file is created outside the tracker; a swap of the locks directory between the confinement check and lock creation is detected by comparing the created lock's identity with the confined directory entry, the stray lock is removed, and the acquisition refuses with lock_path_unsafe; regression tests cover a pre-existing symlinked locks directory and a swap during acquisition for both acquireLock and acquireLockLease; the refusal is documented in docs/SDK.md"
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "New core/lock/lock-confinement.ts: lstat-walk of every component between tracker root and lock parent before mkdir or the cleanup gate (refuses lock_directory_symlink, lock_directory_not_directory, lock_path_outside_tracker); a symlinked lock entry refuses lock_entry_symlink; after open(wx) the handle dev/ino must equal lstat(lockPath) inside the same directory identity, else lock_directory_replaced with Linux procfs stray removal and no unlink of lockPath; pm gc --scope locks refuses a symlinked locks dir. Documented in docs/SDK.md."
expected_result: acquireLock and acquireLockLease never create a lock outside the tracker; symlinked or swapped lock directories refuse with a typed lock_path_unsafe error.
actual_result: "17 confinement specs pass (pre-existing symlink for both entrypoints, non-directory, symlinked entry, swap during acquisition, swap-back with a peer lock preserved, symlinked tracker root works, gc refusal); 101 lock unit tests, full suite and 100% coverage pass."
